WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.600
Andrew: The thing that we talk about a lot
is we don't control the outcome, we don't

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.940
control other people. We just need to focus
on what we do. I think they really embrace

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:18.830
that. They weren't focused on who was ranked
in front of them, who was ranked behind them.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.800
They were focused on what we were going to
do when we were there.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.960
Emily: It was really exciting. Going into
the DMR, we knew we had a shot at winning

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.730
it, so that was on all our minds, but I didn't
want to think about it because I didn't want

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.809
the pressure of "Oh my gosh, we're going to
win." All the girls did such an amazing job

00:00:36.809 --> 00:00:42.420
in the DMR of handing off exactly where the
next leg needed to be. It's been a good experience

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.800
but a hard one for sure.
Andrew: We're really students first and foremost.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.850
A lot of the kids that we compete with are
just athletes.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:57.690
Corinne: I think that being a Hillsdale College
student athlete is just so rewarding, that

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:03.449
you're working hard on and off the track.
Our team motto is excellence, and that's always

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:09.509
what we're trying to pursue at practice, at
the meets, up the hill in the classrooms.

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:13.349
We want to be excellent every day.

